# Tracing one loop turn

```elixir
Mix.install([{:elixir_harness, path: "."}])
```

No instrumentation was added for this. `:dbg` sees every call because
the VM already does — including OTP itself (`:runtime_tools` ships with
every release).

```sh
mix demo.trace
```

```
final: traced
calls observed:
  Session.append/3
  Loop.run/4
  Toon.encode!/1
  Session.to_prompt/1
  Toon.decode/1
```

For live inspection instead of printouts: `:observer.start()` graphs the
same supervision trees mission control renders, and the tracepoints in
`ElixirHarness.Trace` (`@traced`) are the exact seam where a debugger or
`recon` would attach in production.
